Use execute_program({code}) when many tool calls, deterministic multi-step work, or large results can be filtered in one JavaScript program. For a small simple operation or when you need to reason over each result, call the business tool directly.
Program code is an async function body. Call tools[toolId](input) and inspect {observation, sourceReferences}; a successful read_file returns text in result.observation.output. Check observation.kind for every inner call, including failure or rejection. For related files, gather the needed facts in one program and reuse each result within it. Explicitly return one compact JSON-safe conclusion with bounded evidence, not full files or raw observations. Make targeted follow-up calls only for unresolved facts.
For source citations, compute 1-based line numbers from the returned text, return {path, line, text} evidence, and cite only those verified lines in the final answer. When read_file is authorized, for example: const result = await tools.read_file({path:"README.md"}); if (result.observation.kind !== "success") return {error:result.observation.kind}; return {matches:result.observation.output.split("\n").flatMap((text, i) => text.includes("PTC") ? [{path:"README.md", line:i+1, text}] : []).slice(0, 20)};
A program call does not grant its inner tools permission.
